coverage usually needs Netty transport/codec APIs, and the existing test already relies on the HTTP codec stack.\",\n  \"deterministic_setup\": [\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"dependency\",\n      \"coordinate\": \"io.netty:netty-codec-http:5.0.0.Alpha1\",\n      \"scope\": \"testImplementation\",\n      \"reason\": \"Provides the normal Netty HTTP/codec/handler/transport/buffer stack transitively so tests can exercise common utilities through realistic Netty usage.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"agent_guidance\": \"Netty 5.0.0.Alpha1 uses older/incompatible APIs versus recent 4.1/4.2 tests: use methods such as HttpResponse#getStatus(), HttpMessage#getProtocolVersion(), HttpHeaders static helpers, and SimpleChannelInboundHandler#messageReceived(...). Avoid newer APIs like response.status(), response.protocolVersion(), HttpUtil, HttpHeaderNames, and HttpHeaderValues.\",\n  \"risks\": [\n    \"Netty 5.0.0.Alpha1 is very old and API-incompatible with current Netty examples, so generated tests based on modern documentation may fail javac.\"\n  ]\n}", "textSignature": "{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0aae0696135c2090016a748e7b2bf08191a9a4301a92006af0\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}], "api": "openai-codex-responses", "provider": "openai-codex", "model": "gpt-5.5", "usage": {"input": 2244, "output": 1161, "cacheRead": 31232, "cacheWrite": 0, "totalTokens": 34637, "cost": {"input": 0.01122, "output": 0.03483, "cacheRead": 0.015616, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0.061666}}, "stopReason": "stop", "timestamp": 1786023519711, "responseId": "resp_0aae0696135c2090016a748e605dec8191b91a5bdd450433c7"}}
